Bootstrap: docker
From: rockylinux/rockylinux@sha256:8101994123cf3d0a8fee517bee7f39e555c7d92bd2d9eb3303cc988a0eeed00f

# =============================================================================
# bx_atac_motif.1.0
#
#   Target script:
#     - atac_motif.1.0.R
#
#   [MANDATORY BUILD RULES]
#   1) Base OS must be Rocky Linux 9. Rocky 8 is not allowed: it causes
#      environment conflicts on the customer's servers.
#   2) Anaconda Inc. repositories are strictly prohibited. Specifically:
#        - repo.anaconda.com and the defaults / main / r / anaconda channels
#          are never used.
#        - The Anaconda Distribution and the Miniconda installer are never
#          used, because the Miniconda installer is served from
#          repo.anaconda.com and ships defaults-channel packages.
#      conda is therefore provided by Miniforge, which is published by the
#      conda-forge project on GitHub and defaults to the conda-forge channel.
#      Only conda-forge and bioconda (community channels, free-licence, merely
#      hosted on conda.anaconda.org) plus Rocky 9 BaseOS / AppStream are used.
#      Every conda command below passes --override-channels so that no channel
#      outside this list can ever be consulted.
#
#   [TOOL LOCATION]
#   This image installs its tools into the shared prefix /opt/bio (a conda
#   environment), so a tool that appears in more than one image resolves to
#   /opt/bio/bin/<tool>. /opt/bio/bin is first on PATH in %environment. The
#   supplied script calls its tools by name through PATH and needs no
#   change. Do not bind any host path over /opt/bio at runtime.
#
# [PURPOSE]
#   NBIS/monaLisa motif analysis of differential accessibility results:
#   logFC binning, binned motif enrichment against a user-supplied MEME motif
#   database (universalmotif -> TFBSTools PWMs), motif heatmaps and seqLogo
#   PNGs, binned k-mer enrichment, and randomized-lasso stability selection
#   (monaLisa::randLassoStabSel, using stabs and glmnet).
#   The analysis script is supplied through CLOSHA's external bind paths,
#   rather than embedded in the image. This DEF provides its runtime.
#
# [INPUT AND OUTPUT STRUCTURE]
#   Input: input_dir (a differential_accessibility output directory, from
#   which 03_results/diff_accessibility_<norm>.csv is used) or da_csv;
#   genome_fasta with an existing .fai index; motif_db (MEME format);
#   optional norm, chrs, fdr_filter, n_per_bin, min_abs_logfc, padj_cutoff,
#   kmer_len, min_motif_score, stabsel_cutoff, seed, threads, run_kmer,
#   run_regression.
#   Output: 01_qc, 02_binned_enrichment (TSV, RDS, heatmap PDF, seqlogos/
#   PNG), 03_kmer, 04_regression, 05_rds, session_info.txt, and logs/.
#   The script first removes existing output_dir contents except logs/.
#   output_dir must not be an input directory or any parent of an input.
#
# [REQUIRED RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES]
#   R 4.5.3 (conda-forge r-base) and Bioconductor 3.22 packages (bioconda):
#     monaLisa 1.16.0 (with stabs 0.7-1 and glmnet 5.0), BiocParallel,
#     ggplot2 4.0.3, ComplexHeatmap 2.26.1, circlize 0.4.18, GenomicRanges,
#     GenomeInfoDb, IRanges, Rsamtools, TFBSTools 1.48.0 (seqLogo, toICM),
#     universalmotif 1.28.0, SummarizedExperiment, Biostrings; grid (base R).
#   png(type = "cairo") uses the cairo, fontconfig, and conda-forge font
#   packages that r-base pulls in.
#   Every pkg::function call and every unqualified function used after the
#   script's library() calls is checked in %test after the packages load.
#   Runtime analysis needs no network access.
#
# [BASE IMAGE AND INSTALLATION RULES FOR THIS DEF]
#   Base image: the official Rocky Linux 9.8 image
#   rockylinux/rockylinux:9.8.20260525.0, pinned by its index digest in From.
#   conda: Miniforge3-26.7.2-0 (conda-forge project GitHub release),
#   SHA256-checked, used only during the build.
#   Packages: conda-forge and bioconda only, with --override-channels and
#   strict channel priority. Top-level packages are pinned to exact versions;
#   the full resolved set with SHA256 values is recorded in
#   /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif/conda-explicit.txt and checked so that every
#   URL is under conda.anaconda.org/conda-forge or /bioconda.
#   Building requires internet access to github.com and conda.anaconda.org.
#
# [HPC BUILD REQUIREMENTS]
#   Use a designated build environment and an unprivileged build account.
#   Do not run the build as the host root user or through sudo.
#   Do not bind production data or service directories into the build container.
#   Host-side %pre and %setup sections are not used.
#   Package installation and cleanup run inside %post.
#   Build workspace: the fixed container-private path /__closha_build/work.
#   /__closha_build and the workspace are created with plain mkdir (no -p),
#   so the build stops if either already exists, including as a symlink or
#   a bind mount point. The Miniforge installer and its base installation,
#   the conda package cache (CONDA_PKGS_DIRS), the conda configuration file
#   (CONDARC), temporary files (TMPDIR), and HOME for the install steps are
#   all placed below it, so conda itself does not remain in the image; only
#   the /opt/bio environment does.
#   Only the Rocky 9 BaseOS which package is installed with DNF
#   (R's utils package needs /usr/bin/which), with the DNF cache
#   (cachedir) in the workspace and keepcache disabled.
#   Cleanup removes only that exact workspace, after separate checks of the
#   path constant, symlinks, canonical path, and root-filesystem device, and
#   then removes the empty /__closha_build with rmdir. Any failed check stops
#   the build without deleting anything.
#   No wildcard cleanup of default paths is used.
#   These checks reduce accidents but do not prove host isolation. The build
#   service must keep host binds off /__closha_build, its parents, and children.
#   No broad cleanup of /tmp, /var/tmp, /root, or user home directories is used.
#   %test performs checks without creating or deleting data files.
#   The Apptainer output SIF, image cache, and build temporary files are host
#   artifacts; place them in an approved build workspace, separate from services.
#   This DEF does not clean the host's Apptainer cache or build workspace.
#   The build service must enforce account, workspace, and mount restrictions;
#   comments in this DEF cannot enforce the host's bind configuration.
#
# [RUNTIME ENVIRONMENT ISOLATION]
#   Apptainer binds the user's home directory by default. %environment puts
#   /opt/bio/bin first on a PATH without home entries, points R_LIBS_USER at
#   the image library, sets R_PROFILE_USER and R_ENVIRON_USER to /dev/null,
#   and unsets R_LIBS, so that a host ~/R library, ~/.Rprofile, or
#   ~/.Renviron is not loaded into this runtime.
#
# [CHANGES FROM THE PREVIOUS SIF]
#   No previous SIF or DEF for this script was supplied. An earlier draft
#   of this DEF (Ubuntu 24.04, CRAN APT R 4.6.1, Bioconductor 3.23 from
#   source) was replaced before release by this Rocky Linux 9 / Miniforge
#   version; Bioconda currently provides R 4.5.3 and Bioconductor 3.22.
#   This is a new image; nothing existing is modified or overwritten.
#
# [VALIDATION STATUS AND REPRODUCIBILITY]
#   Checked: supplied-script dependencies (library/requireNamespace/::), a
#   dry-run solve of the package set from conda-forge and bioconda only
#   (209 packages), the Miniforge installer SHA256, the Rocky 9.8 base
#   image contents, and DEF %post and %test shell syntax (sh -n).
#   Production /etc/apptainer/apptainer.conf (supplied by the user):
#   mount home/tmp/proc/sys/dev = yes, bind path = /etc/localtime and
#   /etc/hosts, user bind control = yes, allow setuid = yes; Apptainer 1.4.5.
#   Per Apptainer 1.4.5 source (internal/pkg/build, ApplyBuildConfig), %post
#   and %test run with a build config that drops bind path, home,
#   resolv.conf, and devpts but keeps mount tmp, proc, sys, and dev, and
#   APPTAINER_BINDPATH and APPTAINER_MOUNT from the caller still reach them.
#   This DEF therefore fixes PATH, mounts private tmpfs over /tmp and
#   /var/tmp (in %post, and in %test when it runs as root, as it does during
#   builds), prints the mount table, stops before any install step if any
#   mount other than the build defaults is present, and sets HOME, TMPDIR,
#   and XDG directories to the workspace before installing anything. It
#   does not write /etc/hosts, /etc/localtime, /etc/resolv.conf, /dev,
#   /proc, or /sys. These blocks are identical to the ones verified in
#   the ATAC-seq DEFs verified on 2026-09-30 (policy section 6.1).
#   Build from a shell without APPTAINER_* or SINGULARITY_* bind variables.
#   Isolation blocks updated on 2026-10-06 after a production build log: the
#   production build account has no /etc/subuid entry, so Apptainer runs %post
#   under the fakeroot command with read-only helpers under
#   /.singularity.d/libs and the host devtmpfs /dev and /dev/shm. The mount
#   allowlist now accepts those, and /dev/shm is covered with a private tmpfs.
#   Local test builds (2026-10-06, GitHub Codespace, x86_64, Apptainer 1.4.5
#   with the same apptainer.conf as production) succeeded as root, including
#   %test; the --fakeroot rebuild with these blocks is in progress (the
#   previous blocks passed --fakeroot on 2026-10-01). Root builds were traced
#   with strace: no process opened any /proc or /sys path for writing, and host
#   sysctl values did not change. inotify and before/after listings showed no
#   DEF-caused change in the host /tmp or /var/tmp. With --fakeroot, Apptainer
#   itself (fakeroot engine, before %post) creates and immediately removes an
#   empty /tmp/bind-mount-* directory on the host; a DEF cannot prevent it. The
#   fakeroot-command mode was reproduced locally with an account without
#   /etc/subuid entries and a test DEF holding the same %post and %test start
#   blocks on ubuntu:24.04 (the local fakeroot library needs glibc 2.38, newer
#   than Rocky 9); the blocks passed and no file reached the host /tmp or
#   /dev/shm. A full Rocky 9 build in that mode was not possible locally. Built
#   SIF size: 624.6 MiB. The APPTAINER_BINDPATH negative test was run on
#   2026-09-30 with the earlier blocks and was not repeated. Not performed: a
#   build on the production build machine, or analysis of user data.
#   %test checks R 4.5.3, package versions and loading, the functions used by
#   the script, stabs/glmnet, cairo PNG rendering to /dev/null, a file-less PDF
#   device, and the recorded package channels.
#   These checks do not audit the entire filesystem or historical installation
#   activity.
#   Unresolved: the Miniforge and conda package recipe is not yet a
#   registered approved recipe.
#
# [CHANGELOG]
#   2026-10-01 / 1.0: Created for atac_motif.1.0.R on Rocky Linux 9 with
#   Miniforge (conda-forge/bioconda only), following policy 1.4.
# =============================================================================

%labels
    Maintainer       KOBIC Bio-Express
    Pipeline         ATAC-seq
    Component        bx_atac_motif
    Version          1.0
    BaseOS           RockyLinux9
    CondaInstaller   Miniforge3-26.7.2-0
    AnacondaRepoFree true
    RVersion         4.5.3
    Description      "monaLisa environment for the CLOSHA ATAC-seq atac_motif script"

%environment
    export PATH=/opt/bio/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
    export LANG=C.UTF-8
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
    # Keep host-side user R libraries and profiles out of this runtime.
    unset R_LIBS
    export R_LIBS_USER=/opt/bio/lib/R/library
    export R_PROFILE_USER=/dev/null
    export R_ENVIRON_USER=/dev/null

%post
    set -eu
    # Fixed container PATH; ignore any inherited PATH that may point into a
    # host-bound home directory.
    export PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8

    # Apptainer builds keep the admin "mount tmp = yes" setting, so %post sees
    # the host /tmp and /var/tmp. Cover both with private tmpfs mounts in this
    # container's mount namespace before any other command runs; the host
    # directories are then unreachable. If mounting fails, the build stops.
    mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-tmp /tmp
    mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-vartmp /var/tmp
    [ "$(stat -f -c %T /tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
    [ "$(stat -f -c %T /var/tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/var/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
    # With "mount dev = yes" the build may see the host's /dev and its shared
    # /dev/shm. Cover /dev/shm with a private tmpfs as well, then confirm from
    # the mount table that the newest /dev/shm mount is this one.
    if [ -d /dev/shm ]; then
        mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-shm /dev/shm
        awk '$5 == "/dev/shm" { s = $0 } END { exit !(s ~ / - tmpfs closha-shm /) }' /proc/self/mountinfo ||
            { echo "/dev/shm is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
    fi
    # Record the mount table in the build log for review.
    cat /proc/self/mountinfo

    # Stop before any install step if the build container has a mount other
    # than those Apptainer creates for builds: the rootfs, /tmp and /var/tmp
    # (now covered above), private /etc/hosts and /etc/resolv.conf copies, and
    # kernel pseudo-filesystems under /dev, /proc, and /sys, plus, in builds
    # that run %post under the fakeroot command (no /etc/subuid entry), the
    # read-only fakeroot helpers Apptainer places under /.singularity.d/libs.
    # This rejects host paths added through APPTAINER_BINDPATH or
    # APPTAINER_MOUNT, which the build passes into %post from the caller's
    # environment.
    awk '
        { split($0, sep, " - "); split(sep[2], f, " "); mp = $5; opt = $6; fs = f[1]; src = $4 }
        mp == "/" || mp == "/tmp" || mp == "/var/tmp" { next }
        (mp == "/etc/hosts" || mp == "/etc/resolv.conf") &&
            src ~ /\/bundle-temp-[0-9]+\/(hosts|resolv\.conf)$/ { next }
        (mp == "/dev" || mp ~ /^\/dev\//) && fs ~ /^(devtmpfs|tmpfs|devpts|mqueue|hugetlbfs)$/ { next }
        (mp == "/proc" || mp ~ /^\/proc\//) && fs ~ /^(proc|binfmt_misc|autofs)$/ { next }
        (mp == "/sys" || mp ~ /^\/sys\//) &&
            fs ~ /^(sysfs|cgroup|cgroup2|securityfs|selinuxfs|debugfs|tracefs|bpf|fusectl|configfs|pstore|efivarfs)$/ { next }
        mp == "/.singularity.d/libs" && fs == "tmpfs" && opt ~ /^ro(,|$)/ { next }
        mp ~ /^\/\.singularity\.d\/libs\/(fakeroot|faked|libfakeroot\.so)$/ && opt ~ /^ro(,|$)/ { next }
        { print "Unexpected mount in build container: " mp " (" fs ")" > "/dev/stderr"; bad = 1 }
        END { exit bad }
    ' /proc/self/mountinfo || { echo "Build stopped: remove extra bind settings and rebuild" >&2; exit 1; }

    fail() { echo "Build check failed: $*" >&2; exit 1; }

    # Fixed container-private workspace from the approved profile.
    # Plain mkdir (no -p) fails if a path already exists, including a symlink
    # or a bind mount point, so the build stops instead of reusing it.
    BUILD_ROOT=/__closha_build
    WORK=/__closha_build/work
    mkdir -m 0700 -- "$BUILD_ROOT"
    mkdir -m 0700 -- "$WORK"
    mkdir -p -- "$WORK/src" "$WORK/tmp" "$WORK/home" "$WORK/conda-pkgs" "$WORK/dnf-cache"

    # The admin config may bind the host home, and /tmp may be host-backed.
    # Redirect HOME, TMPDIR, and XDG directories into the workspace before any
    # other command runs, so no tool reads or writes host user files or /tmp.
    export HOME="$WORK/home"
    export TMPDIR="$WORK/tmp"
    export XDG_CACHE_HOME="$WORK/home/.cache"
    export XDG_CONFIG_HOME="$WORK/home/.config"
    export XDG_DATA_HOME="$WORK/home/.local/share"

    # The pinned conda packages below are for linux-64 only.
    [ "$(uname -m)" = x86_64 ] || fail "unsupported architecture"
    grep -q '^Rocky Linux release 9\.' /etc/rocky-release || fail "base OS is not Rocky Linux 9"

    # R's utils package runs /usr/bin/which when it loads, and the Rocky 9 base
    # image has no which. Install only that package from Rocky 9 BaseOS, with
    # the DNF cache in the workspace.
    dnf --assumeyes --setopt=cachedir="$WORK/dnf-cache" --setopt=keepcache=0 \
        --setopt=install_weak_deps=False install which
    [ -x /usr/bin/which ] || fail "which was not installed"

    # Miniforge from the conda-forge project's GitHub release (never Miniconda
    # or the Anaconda Distribution). SHA256 matches the published .sha256 file.
    # It is installed into the workspace and removed with it after use.
    curl --fail --location --retry 3 \
        --connect-timeout 30 --max-time 600 \
        --output "$WORK/src/Miniforge3-26.7.2-0-Linux-x86_64.sh" \
        https://github.com/conda-forge/miniforge/releases/download/26.7.2-0/Miniforge3-26.7.2-0-Linux-x86_64.sh
    printf '%s  %s\n' \
        281b0ac7d550802efc81af633225a5e6116d29ae72f3ab4eae7168c3931a4c05 \
        "$WORK/src/Miniforge3-26.7.2-0-Linux-x86_64.sh" | sha256sum --check -
    bash "$WORK/src/Miniforge3-26.7.2-0-Linux-x86_64.sh" -b -p "$WORK/miniforge"

    # conda configuration, package cache, and environments list stay in the
    # workspace. Only conda-forge and bioconda are configured, defaults is
    # empty, and every command still passes --override-channels.
    export CONDARC="$WORK/condarc"
    export CONDA_PKGS_DIRS="$WORK/conda-pkgs"
    printf '%s\n' \
        'channels:' \
        '  - conda-forge' \
        '  - bioconda' \
        'default_channels: []' \
        'channel_priority: strict' \
        'auto_update_conda: false' \
        'notify_outdated_conda: false' \
        'report_errors: false' \
        > "$CONDARC"
    CONDA="$WORK/miniforge/bin/conda"

    # Create the /opt/bio environment from exact package versions.
    "$CONDA" create --yes --prefix /opt/bio \
        --override-channels --channel conda-forge --channel bioconda \
        --strict-channel-priority \
        r-base=4.5.3 \
        bioconductor-monalisa=1.16.0 \
        bioconductor-biocparallel \
        r-ggplot2=4.0.3 \
        bioconductor-complexheatmap=2.26.1 \
        r-circlize=0.4.18 \
        bioconductor-genomicranges \
        bioconductor-genomeinfodb \
        bioconductor-iranges \
        bioconductor-rsamtools \
        bioconductor-tfbstools=1.48.0 \
        bioconductor-universalmotif=1.28.0 \
        bioconductor-summarizedexperiment \
        bioconductor-biostrings \
        r-stabs=0.7_1 \
        r-glmnet=5.0

    # Record the exact package set with SHA256 values, then check that every
    # package came from conda-forge or bioconda.
    mkdir -p /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif
    "$CONDA" list --prefix /opt/bio --explicit --sha256 > /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif/conda-explicit.txt
    awk '
        /^https?:/ && $0 !~ /^https:\/\/conda\.anaconda\.org\/(conda-forge|bioconda)\// { print "Package from a disallowed channel: " $0 > "/dev/stderr"; bad = 1 }
        END { exit bad }
    ' /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif/conda-explicit.txt || fail "package from a disallowed channel"
    "$CONDA" list --prefix /opt/bio > /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif/conda-packages.txt
    cp /etc/rocky-release /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif/base-os-release.txt
    rpm -qa --qf '%{NAME}\t%{VERSION}-%{RELEASE}\n' | sort > /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif/rocky-packages.tsv
    /opt/bio/bin/R --version | head -n 1 > /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif/r-version.txt
    grep -F 'R version 4.5.3' /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif/r-version.txt

    # Remove only the exact workspace created above; stop on any doubt.
    # Each check is a separate command so that set -e cannot skip a failure.
    cd /
    [ "$WORK" = /__closha_build/work ] || fail "unexpected workspace path"
    [ ! -L "$BUILD_ROOT" ] || fail "parent is a symlink"
    [ ! -L "$WORK" ] || fail "workspace is a symlink"
    [ -d "$WORK" ] || fail "workspace is missing"
    [ "$(realpath -e -- "$WORK")" = "$WORK" ] || fail "canonical path changed"
    [ "$(stat -c %d -- "$WORK")" = "$(stat -c %d -- /)" ] || fail "workspace is on another filesystem"
    rm -rf --one-file-system -- "$WORK"
    rmdir -- "$BUILD_ROOT"

%runscript
    exec /opt/bio/bin/Rscript "$@"

%test
    set -eu
    export PATH=/opt/bio/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8

    # The build runs %test separately from %post, again with the host /tmp and
    # /var/tmp bound (mount tmp = yes), and R and Python create temporary
    # files there. When running as root (a root or fakeroot build), cover both,
    # and /dev/shm when present, with private tmpfs mounts first; if mounting
    # fails, the build stops.
    # Unprivileged runtime checks cannot mount and skip this step.
    if [ "$(id -u)" = 0 ]; then
        mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-tmp /tmp
        mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-vartmp /var/tmp
        [ "$(stat -f -c %T /tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
        [ "$(stat -f -c %T /var/tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/var/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
        if [ -d /dev/shm ]; then
            mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-shm /dev/shm
            awk '$5 == "/dev/shm" { s = $0 } END { exit !(s ~ / - tmpfs closha-shm /) }' /proc/self/mountinfo ||
                { echo "/dev/shm is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
        fi
    fi

    for cmd in R Rscript; do
        [ "$(command -v "$cmd")" = "/opt/bio/bin/$cmd" ]
    done
    [ -x /usr/bin/which ]

    R --version | head -n 1 | grep -F 'R version 4.5.3'

    # Attach packages in the script order, then check every pkg::function
    # and every unqualified function the script uses. stabs and glmnet must load
    # (randLassoStabSel), and cairo PNG output with text is rendered to
    # /dev/null so that no file is created.
    Rscript --no-init-file -e '
        pkgs <- c("monaLisa", "BiocParallel", "ggplot2", "ComplexHeatmap",
                  "circlize", "GenomicRanges", "GenomeInfoDb", "IRanges",
                  "Rsamtools", "TFBSTools", "universalmotif", "SummarizedExperiment",
                  "Biostrings", "grid")
        for (p in pkgs) suppressPackageStartupMessages(library(p, character.only = TRUE))
        if (!startsWith(as.character(packageVersion("monaLisa")), "1.16.")) {
            stop("unexpected monaLisa version: ", packageVersion("monaLisa"))
        }
        if (!startsWith(as.character(packageVersion("TFBSTools")), "1.48.")) {
            stop("unexpected TFBSTools version: ", packageVersion("TFBSTools"))
        }
        if (!startsWith(as.character(packageVersion("universalmotif")), "1.28.")) {
            stop("unexpected universalmotif version: ", packageVersion("universalmotif"))
        }
        used <- c(
            "Rsamtools::FaFile", "Rsamtools::scanFaIndex",
            "Rsamtools::scanFa", "GenomicRanges::seqnames",
            "GenomicRanges::GRanges", "GenomicRanges::trim",
            "GenomicRanges::resize", "IRanges::width",
            "IRanges::IRanges", "BiocParallel::MulticoreParam",
            "GenomeInfoDb::keepSeqlevels", "GenomeInfoDb::renameSeqlevels",
            "GenomeInfoDb::seqlevels", "GenomeInfoDb::seqlengths<-",
            "Biostrings::alphabetFrequency", "universalmotif::read_meme",
            "universalmotif::convert_motifs", "TFBSTools::PWMatrixList",
            "TFBSTools::Matrix"
        )
        for (u in used) {
            x <- strsplit(u, "::", fixed = TRUE)[[1]]
            invisible(getExportedValue(x[1], x[2]))
        }
        unqualified <- c(
            "seqlevels", "seqnames", "mcols", "mcols<-",
            "width", "bin", "plotBinDensity", "plotBinDiagnostics",
            "calcBinnedMotifEnrR", "assay", "rowData", "colData",
            "motifSimilarity", "plotMotifHeatmaps", "seqLogo", "toICM",
            "calcBinnedKmerEnr", "motifKmerSimilarity", "seqLogoGrob", "rowAnnotation",
            "annoSeqlogo", "draw", "Heatmap", "colorRamp2",
            "findMotifHits", "oligonucleotideFrequency", "randLassoStabSel", "plotStabilityPaths",
            "plotSelectionProb", "ggplot", "aes", "geom_histogram",
            "xlab", "ylab", "theme_bw", "ggsave",
            "gpar", "unit"
        )
        missing <- unqualified[!vapply(unqualified, exists, logical(1))]
        if (length(missing) > 0) {
            stop("functions not found on the search path: ", paste(missing, collapse = ", "))
        }
        for (p in c("stabs", "glmnet")) {
            if (!requireNamespace(p, quietly = TRUE)) stop(p, " is not installed")
        }
        if (!isTRUE(capabilities("cairo"))) stop("R cairo support is not available")
        png(filename = "/dev/null", width = 300, height = 150, type = "cairo")
        plot(1, main = "cairo text")
        invisible(dev.off())
        pdf(NULL)
        plot(1)
        invisible(dev.off())
        cat("monaLisa", as.character(packageVersion("monaLisa")), "\n")
    '

    # Every recorded package URL must come from conda-forge or bioconda.
    awk '
        /^https?:/ && $0 !~ /^https:\/\/conda\.anaconda\.org\/(conda-forge|bioconda)\// { print "Package from a disallowed channel: " $0 > "/dev/stderr"; bad = 1 }
        END { exit bad }
    ' /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif/conda-explicit.txt
    [ "$(grep -c -E '^https://' /opt/bio/share/bx-atac-motif/conda-explicit.txt)" -gt 0 ]

    # The build workspace must not remain in the image.
    if [ -e /__closha_build ]; then
        echo 'Build workspace /__closha_build remains in the image' >&2
        exit 1
    fi

    echo 'R 4.5.3 / Bioconductor 3.22 (bioconda): bx_atac_motif runtime dependency checks passed.'

%help
    CLOSHA ATAC motif environment: R 4.5.3 + Bioconductor 3.22 (monaLisa,
    TFBSTools, universalmotif, ComplexHeatmap, circlize, Rsamtools, Biostrings,
    BiocParallel, stabs, glmnet, ggplot2).
    Base OS: Rocky Linux 9. Tools are installed in /opt/bio from conda-forge and
    bioconda with Miniforge; no Anaconda Inc. repository or Miniconda is used.

    The CLOSHA build service builds this DEF with its fixed Slurm job (policy
    section 6.2), on an internet-connected x86_64 node, without extra binds:
        apptainer build bx_atac_motif.1.0.sif bx_atac_motif.1.0.def
    It must pass both as root and with fakeroot.

    Store the SIF, Apptainer cache, and build temporary files in an approved host
    build workspace. APPTAINER_CACHEDIR and APPTAINER_TMPDIR select the cache and
    temporary directories. Container cleanup must never target host-backed binds.
    Build from a shell without APPTAINER_* or SINGULARITY_* bind variables.

    Check the image:
        apptainer test --cleanenv bx_atac_motif.1.0.sif

    atac_motif.1.0.R is supplied externally through approved runtime binds.
    This DEF does not run it during image construction:
        apptainer exec bx_atac_motif.1.0.sif Rscript atac_motif.1.0.R key=value ...

    genome_fasta must already have a .fai index (the script stops otherwise).
    The script removes previous output except logs/, so output_dir must be
    separate from the inputs and their parents. That existing deletion behavior
    must be reviewed separately before service use.
    Writable runtime binds can expose host data to the analysis script.
    Runtime analysis requires no network access.
